  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Convening Fund: Strategic Science &amp; Tech Reporting: Enhancing Nigerian Media Capacity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to strengthen the capacity of Nigerian media to deliver strategic, impactful reporting that positions science and technology as critical drivers of economic growth&#x2014;aligned with the UK Foreign Secretary&#x2019;s core priorities. Through a comprehensive approach combining journalist training, institutional capacity building, and sustainable network development, the initiative seeks to elevate the quality and influence of science and technology narratives in the Nigerian media landscape. Key objectives include; 
Advanced Journalist Training: Equip 45 journalists&#x2014;including partners of the British High Commission Abuja&#x2014;with in-depth knowledge and practical skills to understand, analyse, and report on the role of science and technology in driving economic growth.
International Exposure &amp; Knowledge Exchange: Organise UK institutional visits for selected journalists to experience global journalism standards and innovative storytelling techniques, fostering cross-border learning.
Sustainable Media Partnerships: Build enduring collaborations among media professionals, government agencies, and research institutions, creating platforms for dialogue and joint reporting on science and technology issues.</narrative>
  </description>
